    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0448" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11W892/1992</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Undersecretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of a Telephone
                        Conversation With the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von
                        Prittwitz</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1931</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-18">November 18, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The German Ambassador telephoned me to say that he had communicated with his
                    Government in relation to the possible appointment of an umpire<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d358-f1"/> for the Mixed Claims Commission and that his Government
                    fully supported the agreement we had reached here, that it would not be
                    necessary at the moment to appoint an umpire. He said his Government felt the
                    American and German Commissioners might be able to reach an agreement without an
                    umpire, but if they could not do so, they could at least so closely define the
                    questions at <pb facs="0449" n="329" xml:id="pg329"/> issue that an umpire would
                    have a narrow question only to decide. He felt, as I do, that if the
                    Commissioners found they could not reach an agreement, it will be easy to decide
                    very promptly on the umpire.…</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d358-f1" n="57" xml:id="d358-f1-content">
                <p>Roland W. Boyden, Umpire, died on October 25, 1931. He was succeeded by Mr.
                    Justice Owen J. Roberts, of the Supreme Court of the United States, appointed
                    March 24, 1932.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
